#  Database — MySQL
docker run -d \
  -p 3306:3306 \
  --name mysql-db \
  -e MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=mypassword \
  -e MYSQL_DATABASE=mydb \
  -v mysql-data:/var/lib/mysql \
  mysql:latest
  
 # -e for environment variables (password, db name)
 # -v for volume (so data survives if container restarts)
No need to expose database to public — usually kept internal hence we dont use port mapping here.



Flag      Purpose 	       Web-app        Database
-d      Run in background        Always       Always

-p      Port mapping           Required       But keep internal

--name  Give it a name 		Always        Always

-e      Environment variables  Sometimes      Always (passwords)

-v      volume for data         Rarely        Always

--network Connect containers   Sometimes      When app needs DB
